<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold mb-3">Dispensing &amp; Verification</h1>
        <p class="lead mb-4">
            A counter-first workstation that turns prescriptions into verified, labelled, and
            billed dispenses — with permanent script numbers, clinical safety cues, and a clear
            path from Save to Collect or POS.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Quick Dispense workflow</h2>
        <p>
            Select till and currency, then search or register the patient. Allergies, chronic
            notes, and medical-aid membership appear before medicines are added. Choose a
            doctor or referrer from the local register or MDPCZ public directory. Add line items
            with product search, quantity, price, dosage cypher (BD, TDS, and more), dose, days
            supply, auto-expanded directions, and optional refill schedules.
        </p>
        <p>
            Attach the doctor’s script as a photo or PDF — including in-browser camera capture —
            so the paper trail stays with the digital record. Keyboard shortcuts keep high-volume
            counters moving: save, verify, and collect without leaving the workstation.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Pharmacist verification and labels</h2>
        <p>
            Status advances Dispensed → Verified → Collected (or Awaiting POS for shortfalls).
            Verification is a deliberate pharmacist step, not an afterthought. Print medicine
            labels with dosage text derived from cyphers, and generate dispense PDFs for patient
            or audit packs.
        </p>
        <p>
            Hold, cancel, or return paths keep exception handling inside the same document —
            protecting stock accuracy and the audit trail when a script cannot leave the counter.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Payment without a second system</h2>
        <p>
            Collect cash, card, or medical aid at the pharmacy workstation, or send unpaid
            shortfalls to POS. Dispenses are invoice documents with real <code>RX-</code> numbers
            assigned at create time — status changes never mint a temporary ID that confuses
            patients or staff at pickup.
        </p>
        <p>
            Dispensing records provide searchable history with print-label and print-PDF actions
            for every completed script, supporting both retail counters and hospital dispensaries.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

